Backport the two-line runtime fix from vllm-project/vllm#64141 (5db1c89c64f0),
by yueyinmochen, for vllm-project/vllm#63944. Creating quantized attention's
scale aliases must not initialize the whole pool: hybrid groups can already
own pages containing live recurrent state, and KV-sharing layers can already
have valid scales there. PTH_FA inherits these view methods from Triton.

New KV writes store their scales with their values; masked attention loads use
their own out-of-range defaults. This patch does not initialize dummy/capture
pages or change those kernels' validity/masking contracts.

Kind: backport
What: create per-token-head scale views without filling shared KV pages, preserving live hybrid state and existing scales
Upstream: vllm #64141 (open), fixing #63944; runtime change credited to yueyinmochen
Cut-against: 0.33.0
Retires-when: the pin carries vllm #64141 or an equivalent non-destructive scale-view implementation

